      en: ["Housed in the neoclassical Municipal Palace built in 1910.", "Features the original Act of Separation from Colombia (1903).", "Includes a collection of pre-Columbian ceramics and tools.", "Exhibits on the different flags used throughout Panama's history.", "Provides context for the 1964 student protests (Martyrs' Day).", "Managed by the Ministry of Culture.", "Essential for understanding Panama's complex relationship with Colombia and the US.", "A primary resource for students and historians."]
